# ai_context.md routine (confluence-lab)

`ai_context.md` (repo root) is the compact state summary used to start
fresh chats cheaply in THIS workspace. It must never go stale.

This repo is a standalone research lab, fully separate from the trading
agent repo (`eurusd-ai-agent`). Never write lab docs, reports, results or
tests into the agent repo, and never import lab code into it. The only
allowed coupling is read-only use of the agent's data cache via PYTHONPATH.

## When starting a fresh session

If the user references `@ai_context.md` or asks "where did we leave off",
read it FIRST, then `REPORT.md` / `PROTOCOL.md` for depth. Do not re-derive
history from code or old chats.

## When to UPDATE it (proactively, don't wait to be asked)

- A study stage completes or a verdict registry changes.
- A protocol is pre-registered or amended.
- The user signals the session is ending ("summarize", "brain dump",
  "starting fresh", "closing this thread").

## How to update it

Keep the three-section structure (what is built / key paths / next goal),
exact numbers, < 90 lines. Bump the date in the header. Statistical
honesty rules (pre-registration, FDR accounting, no post-freeze retuning,
negative results reported) are part of the state — keep them visible.

After updating, tell the user it was updated. Commit `ai_context.md`
together with the work it describes (when the user asks for a commit).
